    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm doing an accessibility audit for a fintech app we're launching. can you give me a quick checklist for WCAG 2.1 compliance focusing on color contrast ratios and screen reader compatibility? thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely! For WCAG 2.1 compliance related to color contrast, ensure that your text and background color contrast ratios meet at least AA (AV 4.5:1 for normal text and AV 3:1 for large text). Use tools like the WebAIM Contrast Checker to evaluate your elements. For screen reader compatibility, meaningful titles and labels should be used for form inputs, employs proper heading hierarchy for structuring content, and navigate flat text should be identifiable by their semantic elements like 'header', 'footer', and 'article'. Additionally, it’s good to implement focus indicators and ensure that all interactive elements are keyboard accessible.",
