    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i get that. but manually testing takes forever. is there any specific way to categorize these \"hidden\" bugs so we can tell the devs exactly what's wrong? like, is there a better way to describe those small, annoying little errors that just pop up out of nowhere and mess with the user flow?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To categorize and communicate hidden bugs effectively, use a detailed reporting template that encourages descriptive and precise language. Break down each issue by providing the following: context of the problem (what the user was doing), exact user path to reproduce the glitch (step-by-step actions), any observed visual anomalies, and the impact on accessibility (e.g., how it affects keyboard navigation or screen reader interpretation). Adding screenshots, screen recordings, or even short video clips can be incredibly helpful. Use tags or categories for common types of issues to streamline the communication process. This categorization not only aids developers in understanding the severity and nature of the problems but also in pinpointing their resolution. Encourage developers to create a workflow where they also describe the potential root causes or factors contributing to the bug that can help prevent similar issues in the future.",
      "source": "target",
